1
00:04:17,142 --> 00:04:23,142
A soaring experience unlike anything you've ever seen before.

2
00:08:34,285 --> 00:08:40,285
Birdy is a drama, war film directed by Alan Parker.

3
00:12:51,428 --> 00:12:57,428
Two young men are seriously affected by the Vietnam War.

4
00:17:08,571 --> 00:17:14,571
One of them has always been obsessed with birds - but now believes he
really is a bird, and has been sent to a mental hospital.

5
00:21:25,714 --> 00:21:31,714
Can his friend help him pull through?

6
00:25:42,857 --> 00:25:48,857
Birdy, played by Matthew Modine.

7
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Sergeant Al Columbato, played by Nicolas Cage.

8
00:34:17,142 --> 00:34:23,142
Doctor Major Weiss, played by John Harkins.

9
00:38:34,285 --> 00:38:40,285
Mr. Columbato, played by Sandy Baron.

10
00:42:51,428 --> 00:42:57,428
Hannah Rourke, played by Karen Young.

11
00:47:08,571 --> 00:47:14,571
Renaldi, played by Bruno Kirby.

12
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
Birdy is a 1984 American drama film based on William
Wharton's 1978 novel of the same name.

13
00:55:42,857 --> 00:55:48,857
Directed by Alan Parker, it stars Matthew Modine and Nicolas Cage.

14
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Set in 1960s Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, the film focuses on the friendship
between two teenage boys, Birdy (Modine) and Al Columbato (Cage).

15
01:04:17,142 --> 01:04:23,142
The story is presented in flashbacks, with a frame narrative depicting
their traumatic experiences serving in the Vietnam War.

16
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
Parker initially turned down an opportunity to direct, believing that the
complex book could not be successfully adapted for a feature film.

17
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
The project resurfaced in 1982 when A&M Films, a subsidiary of A&M Records, acquired the film
rights and commissioned Sandy Kroopf and Jack Behr to write the screenplay.

18
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
Upon reading the script, Parker returned as director, and the
film continued development at Tri-Star Pictures.

19
01:21:25,714 --> 01:21:31,714
Principal photography began in May 1984 and concluded in August of that year.

20
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
Filming took place on locations in Philadelphia and Santa Clara, California.

21
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The film is notable for being the first to be partially shot with the Skycam, a
computer-controlled camera system created by Steadicam inventor Garrett Brown.

22
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
The score was composed by Peter Gabriel.

23
01:38:34,285 --> 01:38:40,285
Birdy opened in limited release on December 12, 1984.

24
01:42:51,428 --> 01:42:57,428
It underperformed at the North American box office, grossing
only $1.4 million against a budget of $12 million.

25
01:47:08,571 --> 01:47:14,571
The film received mostly positive reviews, and has an
approval rating of 83% at Rotten Tomatoes.

26
01:51:25,714 --> 01:51:31,714
Birdy was chosen by the National Board of Review as one of the Top Ten Films of 1984, and
won the Grand Prix Spécial du Jury prize at the 1985 Cannes Film Festival.

27
01:55:42,857 --> 01:55:48,857
The tone is emotional.
